{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin. it's based on the book \"the facebook effect\" by ben mezrich.\n\nthe film starts with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, who creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets zuckerberg in trouble with the university.\n\nlater, zuckerberg is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are also students at harvard, with an idea to create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees to work on the project, but eventually drops the winklevoss twins and starts working on his own version of the site with his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield).\n\nthe site, which is initially called \"thefacebook,\" quickly becomes popular and spreads to other colleges and universities. however, the success of the site also leads to a lot of conflicts and lawsuits, including a lawsuit filed by the winklevoss twins and another one filed by eduardo saverin, who claims that zuckerberg cheated him out of his share of the company.\n\nthe film is well-acted, with jesse eisenberg delivering a standout performance as mark zuckerberg. he perfectly captures the character's awkwardness and intensity, and brings a lot of depth to the role. the supporting cast is also excellent, with andrew garfield and armie hammer delivering memorable performances.\n\nthe direction by david fincher is also noteworthy. he uses a lot of dark and moody lighting to create a sense of tension and unease, which perfectly captures the mood of the film. the cinematography is also excellent, with a lot of clever camera angles and compositions that add to the overall visual style of the film.\n\nthe screenplay by aaron sorkin is also excellent. he uses a lot of witty and clever dialogue to bring the characters to life, and the script is full of clever references and allusions to the world of technology and social media. the film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy, with a lot of haunting and atmospheric soundscapes that perfectly capture the mood of the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-made and engaging film that tells a fascinating story about the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. it's a must-see for anyone interested in technology, social media, or just great storytelling in general.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11599371582269669}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.406679530191468e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.033069949597120285}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.406679530191468e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24417318403720856}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05251261964440346}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.15761412680149078}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -9.536788638797589e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.529963462118758e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.01697465591132641}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00015569945389870554}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0788910835981369}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0001918857597047463}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08118155598640442}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.13300925493240356}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0017668110085651278}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.003694017417728901}, {"